  "summary_text": "Kyle,\n\nPort Washington is running strong with real performance gains. Yesterday's 24% revenue jump reflects both solid capacity utilization\u2014four groomers at $468/day, slightly below the 30-day baseline of $513 but offset by elevated bather hours (7.6h vs 5.3h avg)\u2014and disciplined upselling: add-on attach improved to 67% from 56% week-over-week. Month-to-date, you're 3.7% ahead of the DOW-adjusted expectation, and retail jumped 61% yesterday. The YTD picture is exceptional: 50% revenue growth on 52% more appointments shows the location is scaling efficiently. One note: retail inventory is bleeding (X-Small Treat Table and bully sticks negative), and your lapse pool of 486 customers represents $310K in reactivation opportunity\u2014worth a targeted campaign.\n\nHicksville presents a mixed signal. Yesterday's 133% revenue spike looks dramatic until you factor in the comparison base: last Saturday was brutally weak ($708). The real driver was grooming capacity\u2014four groomers producing $370/day, modestly below baseline\u2014executing at 13 grooms. But add-on attach collapsed to 15% from 50%, and retail dropped 52%. This is operational slippage, not calendar. More concerning: visit-cadence drift is growing (12+ week bucket up 1.8 points), an early warning that customers are spacing out. Retail inventory is also critical: you're negative on two fast-moving items (Treat Table, Cannoli). Month-to-date, you're ahead of DOW-adjusted expectation (+12%), so the trend is positive, but the attach-rate and cadence signals warrant attention.\n\n**Capacity & coverage:** Port Washington has 0 groomers scheduled today (Sunday), 3 tomorrow with 7h bathers each day; Hicksville has 0 today, 1 tomorrow with no bathers; across the next 7 days you have 35 groomer-days scheduled (26 Port, 9 Hicksville) and 43 bather hours (all Port)."
